  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The outer zone – 3v3 with jokers on the wings",
  "description": "Split the court into a playing zone in the middle and two narrow outer zones along the boards, about 2 metres wide. Play 3v3 in the playing zone. 1–2 jokers (J) in the outer zones play for whichever team has the ball, for example one on each half.\n\nThe attacking team must pass to a joker before they may shoot. Goals can also be scored straight from an outer zone. Young players tend to crowd around the ball – this game teaches them to use the width and link up play.\n\nPlay for example 2 × 5 minutes and change jokers. Keep balls by the goals so the goalkeeper can restart quickly when the ball goes out. Play lengthwise or across the court depending on age – never on the full court.\n\nProgression: jokers in the outer zone may tackle each other, or remove the jokers and give extra points for goals that come via an outer zone.\n\nNot to scale. The goalkeepers are not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Spread out – make the middle bigger by not crowding the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Jokers: move along the boards so the ball carrier can always find you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass out to the outer zone when the opponents have bunched up in the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: try to reach a player in the outer zone straight away when restarting."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
